DEFINITIONS

"Discovery" means the source code, build files, assets and compiled mod files in this repository.

"Official build" means a compiled Discovery mod file published by Kalpe Games (on its Modrinth
project page or in this repository's releases), exactly as published.

"The Service" means serverlist.cc and its APIs, including api.serverlist.cc, operated by
Kalpe Games.

"You" means any person or organisation exercising rights under this license.


1. READING AND BUILDING THE SOURCE

You may read and study the source code, and build it, for your own personal use: to check what
Discovery does, to debug it, or to prepare a contribution to this repository (section 5).


2. REDISTRIBUTING OFFICIAL BUILDS

You may include official builds in modpacks, launchers, game clients and mod lists, free or paid,
as long as:

  a. the mod file is unmodified: not recompiled, patched, repackaged, obfuscated, shaded, nested
     inside or merged into another file;
  b. you do not ship settings or files that hide, skip or pre-dismiss Discovery's first-run
     notice about play stats, turn play stats on for anyone who has turned them off, or
     otherwise keep from players what Discovery does. You may ship Discovery's other settings
     (for example its layout options);
  c. Discovery, Kalpe Games and this license stay credited wherever your product lists the mods
     it includes;
  d. you do not sell Discovery on its own, or suggest that Kalpe Games endorses, sponsors or
     supports your product without written permission.

Players may change any of Discovery's own in-game settings.


3. NO MODIFIED VERSIONS OR DERIVATIVE WORKS

You may not distribute, publish, host or otherwise make available any modified version of
Discovery, or any work based on it. In particular, you may not:

  a. change its appearance, layout, styling, text or branding;
  b. make it connect to any service other than the Service, or change, redirect, proxy, cache,
     replay or add to the requests it makes to the Service;
  c. port it to another mod loader, game version or platform yourself;
  d. use any part of its source code, assets or design in another mod, client, launcher or
     program.

Changes you make for your own private use are allowed as long as they are never distributed and
the modified copy still talks only to the Service, unchanged.


